Firefox video on the overlay plane: no window drawing while only the video changes (A1b)

On top of 0006 (docs/design/firefox-video-overlay.md §2.3 point 4, §6 step 4).
WebRender marks a compositor surface's whole rect dirty on every frame. While
SwCompositor has the surface on the overlay plane, its new pictures change
nothing in the window, so the renderer (calculate_dirty_rects) leaves it out of
the dirty rects: a frame in which only the video changed has an empty dirty
rect, SwCompositor composites nothing, RenderCompositorSWGL draws nothing into
the widget, and app_server copies nothing; the plane is still flipped
(Compositor::plane_rect, new; default None).

When other content over the video's rect changes (the controls fading in, a
caption), the renderer keeps the video dirty and tells the compositor
(Compositor::plane_covered): the video is composited in software until the
content over it has been still for 0.5 s, so translucent content blends with
the picture rather than with the key. A frame the plane declines after being
left out keeps the plane's previous picture for that frame (the window still
holds the key); the next frame is dirty again and goes in software.

An empty dirty rect now clips every surface out in SwCompositor (before, it
composited the whole window into a dummy framebuffer); it only happens here.

